  "term": "madness",
  "definition": "Madness is presented here as a historically discussed form of human experience, including experiences like hearing voices, whose meaning has often been overridden by biomedical psychiatry. In this context, the term highlights how people’s own understanding of these experiences can be dismissed or silenced.",
